README – mtcars Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

This script performs a complete exploratory data analysis (EDA) of the mtcars dataset using R. It includes data inspection, descriptive statistics, visualizations, outlier detection, correlation analysis, and group comparisons.

What the Code Does
1. Load Data & Libraries

Loads tidyverse, ggplot2, and corrplot, then imports the mtcars dataset into df.

2. Initial Data Exploration

Checks structure (str) and summary statistics (summary).

Identifies missing values and visualizes missingness.

3. Descriptive Statistics

Calculates mean, median, and standard deviation for all numeric variables.

4. Data Visualization

Creates:

Histograms for mpg, wt, and hp

Boxplots for mpg, disp, and qsec

Scatterplot of mpg vs wt with trend line

Scatterplot of mpg vs hp colored by number of cylinders

Boxplot of mpg by transmission type (am)

5. Outlier Detection

Uses the IQR method to detect outliers in all numeric variables.

6. Correlation Analysis

Computes a correlation matrix.

Visualizes correlations using corrplot.

Extracts the three strongest positive/negative correlations.

7. Group Analysis

Compares mpg across:

Number of cylinders (4, 6, 8)

Transmission type (automatic vs manual)

8. Statistical Testing & Modeling

Performs a t-test to assess if mpg differs by transmission.

Builds a multiple regression model (mpg ~ wt + hp + cyl) to identify key predictors.

Summary of Insights

Heavier and more powerful cars have lower fuel efficiency (mpg).

Transmission type matters: manual cars achieve significantly higher mpg.

Weight is the strongest predictor of mpg.

Cars with 8 cylinders consume more fuel than 4- or 6-cylinder cars.
